.TH RECONFOX 1 "2026-07-21" "reconfox 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reconfox \- reconnaissance toolkit for authorized security testing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reconfox
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B reconfox scan
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITARGET\fR...
.br
.B reconfox diff
\fIOLD.json\fR \fINEW.json\fR
.br
.B reconfox doctor
.br
.B reconfox schema
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reconfox
automates the first phase of an authorized penetration test. Given one or more
targets it enumerates subdomains, resolves the host, inspects TLS, scans ports
with
.BR nmap ,
fingerprints HTTP, fuzzes web content with
.BR ffuf ,
runs
.B nuclei
templates and looks up known exploits, then writes a single report
(HTML, Markdown, JSON, NDJSON or SARIF).
.PP
Stages run on a generic dependency-ordered engine: independent stages run
concurrently and a failing non-critical stage is isolated rather than aborting
the run. Running without a subcommand opens a Textual TUI.
.PP
.B reconfox is for legal use only:
your own systems, engagements with written authorization, training ranges
(DVWA, Metasploitable, HackTheBox, TryHackMe) and CTFs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan \fITARGET\fR...
Scan one or more targets. Targets may be URLs/hostnames, a file
.RB ( -iL ),
standard input
.RB ( - ),
or CIDR ranges (expanded to hosts, capped at 4096).
.TP
.B diff \fIOLD.json NEW.json\fR
Compare two JSON reports and show what appeared/disappeared (subdomains, ports,
web findings, vulnerabilities). With
.B --fail-on-change
exits 3 when anything changed \(em useful for cron monitoring.
.TP
.B doctor
Report which external tools (nmap, ffuf, searchsploit, nuclei) are installed,
with versions, and whether the wordlist exists. Exits 1 if a required tool
(nmap/ffuf) is missing \(em suitable as a CI preflight.
.TP
.B schema
Print the JSON Schema of a scan result (\fBScanResult\fR) so downstream
automation can validate the JSON/NDJSON output.
.SH SCAN OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " [quick|full|stealth]"
nmap profile. quick = top-100 ports (\fB-T4 -F -sV\fR); full = all ports
(\fB-T4 -p- -sV -sC\fR); stealth = SYN + fragmentation (\fB-T2 -sS -f -sV\fR).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIDIR\fR"
Directory for report files (default: \fB./reports\fR).
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-output\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Exact output path; format from the extension. \fB-O -\fR writes to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " [md|html|json|sarif|all]"
Report format(s).
.TP
.BR \-iL ", " \-\-target\-file " \fIPATH\fR"
Read targets from a file, one per line.
.TP
.B \-\-subdomains
Enumerate subdomains (crt.sh + DNS bruteforce). Opt-in (third party + DNS noise).
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-subdomains
Enumerate subdomains and run the full pipeline against each discovered host.
.TP
.B \-\-nuclei
Active template-based vulnerability scan. Intrusive \(em opt-in only.
.TP
.B \-\-metasploit
Look up modules via msfrpcd instead of searchsploit (read-only). Requires
.B MSF_RPC_PASS
to be set to a non-default value.
.TP
.B \-\-enrich
Enrich geo/ASN via ip-api.com. Off by default (OPSEC: leaks the target IP to a
third party over plaintext). Use
.B \-\-proxy
to route that traffic.
.TP
.B \-\-scope " \fICIDR\fR"
Allow-list; a target whose resolved IP is outside every range is refused. May be
given multiple times.
.TP
.B \-\-out\-of\-scope " \fICIDR\fR"
Deny-list; a target whose resolved IP falls inside any range is refused.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-private
Permit scanning private/internal IPs (127.0.0.1, RFC1918, link-local) and
redirects to them. By default such targets are refused (DNS-rebind / SSRF guard).
.TP
.B \-\-ndjson
Stream findings to stdout as NDJSON (one JSON object per line); human output
goes to stderr, keeping stdout pipe-clean.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on " [info|low|medium|high|critical]"
Exit 3 if any finding is at or above this severity (CI gate).
.TP
.BR \-\-threads ", " \-\-rate
ffuf threads / requests-per-second cap.
.TP
.BR \-\-nmap\-min\-rate ", " \-\-nmap\-max\-rate ", " \-\-scan\-delay
nmap speed tuning.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout " \fISECONDS\fR"
Per-scanner timeout (default depends on mode). A hung tool is killed.
.TP
.B \-\-wordlist " \fIPATH\fR"
ffuf wordlist (falls back to a seclists path if the default is missing).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show every step.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tui
Headless mode (no TUI).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or partial success with warnings).
.TP
.B 1
Every scanned target failed.
.TP
.B 2
Argument error (bad target, bad CIDR, unknown output extension).
.TP
.B 3
A
.B \-\-fail\-on
threshold was met, or
.B diff \-\-fail\-on\-change
detected a change.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/reconfox/config.toml
Default configuration ([scan]/[diff] tables). Precedence: CLI flag > env
(\fBRECONFOX_*\fR) > config > built-in default.
.TP
.I /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt
Default ffuf wordlist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MSF_RPC_HOST, MSF_RPC_PORT, MSF_RPC_USER, MSF_RPC_PASS, MSF_RPC_SSL
Metasploit RPC connection settings for
.BR --metasploit .
reconfox refuses to connect with an empty or the well-known default
.RB ( changeme )
password.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Quick scan, Markdown report:
.PP
.RS
.B reconfox scan https://example.com --no-tui
.RE
.PP
Full scan with subdomains and nuclei, all report formats:
.PP
.RS
.B reconfox scan https://example.com -m full --scan-subdomains --nuclei -f all --no-tui
.RE
.PP
Several targets, NDJSON into a pipe:
.PP
.RS
.B reconfox scan a.com b.com 10.0.0.0/24 --ndjson --no-tui | jq .
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR ffuf (1),
.BR nuclei (1),
.BR searchsploit (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Fedor Zuev (kovanZ1). Source: https://github.com/kovanZ1/reconfox
.SH SECURITY
